This is because you over-used force bolt spell.  Loud noises
wake up sleeping monsters like nymphs or thrown room
court monsters and then they start wandering the level
attacking you when they see you.

> i only luckily was teleported across the room
> to the one with an up stair with a tele scroll (i wanted to go up
> cause my pet was up there). How do I manage these monsters? I've never
> seen so many...this a throne room only thing?

It will happen if you wake up any group of sleepers so
it will also happen with a barricks.

> Second...i can take a few large mimics or small ones, but my pet cant.
> How do I get my dog to stay back? i cant lure them out, or else my pet
> will get itself killed first...so I basically can't use the shop at
> all.

If you can take out the mimics, your pet is willing to attack
them, but your pet loses in combat to them, then your pet
is close to having the strength to kill them.  You could close
the door, explore a few more levels, then go back to the shop
and let your pet lose.  Alternately enter the shop, close the
door with your pet outside, take out the mimics one by one
until the shop is clear of them, then open the door to let your
pet in.

> I'm a lvl 9 Wizard on DLvl8, farthest I have gotten in a game so far.
> I've basically survived on Force Bolt and my pet for everything, but I
> simply don't have enough energy to keep casting it on those throne
> room baddies...

You don't mention firing daggers from your quiver or other
missile weapons.  Daggers not force bolt are your primary
early game weapon as soon as you start picking some up.
Conveniently, thrown daggers don't wake up any monster but
the one they are thrown at.

Note how much energy force bolt takes and stop casting it
while you still have enough energy to cast it once.  It is your
most powerful weapon early on so don't run it dry.  Use it
but keep at least one cast in reserve while you throw daggers
or other missiles.


